    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied by the types that have a free <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput> for the formatter. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Satisfied when the call <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt; (formatter, value)</computeroutput> is valid, which looks for free functions only, by argument-dependent lookup, so it does not see the member functions of the formatter. The framework defines no free <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput> for the formatter; the ones found are those of the application. They take precedence over the templates of the formatter for the scoped enumerations and for the types with <computeroutput>begin()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>end()</computeroutput>, which would be written by the formatter if the application did not define its own function, so that the application controls the text of its type.</para>
